      "content": "Thanks for this. It's a good start, but I'm a bit worried it might not rank high enough for the \"thoroughness\" check. The tool is pretty sensitive to the number of distinct headers it detects—it basically flags anything with just a few broad sections as \"not comprehensive.\"\n\nCan you expand on the methodology critique specifically? I need it to be much more granular. For example, instead of just one \"Methodology\" section, maybe break it down into the different specific steps of their process so the critique is more targeted. Just make sure it's still actually useful, I don't want it to be fluff.",
